{{!-- WHAT A SEASON IS CALLED, WHEREVER IT IS PRINTED.

      One heading, two hosts: the block on a single-track spine, and the row head on the aggregate
      board. They lay their surroundings out differently but they name a season the same way, and
      when this was written out twice the two could drift -- which on a chronicle means the same
      season reading as two different ones depending on which view you opened.

      ⚠ THE COLOUR IS THE HOST'S, NOT THIS HEADING'S. Each host wears the period's `seasonClass`,
      which paints it in the timeline's own season colour (never the four `--stonetop-season-*-ink`
      tokens, which belong to the steading header's clock; a test counts every read of them). The
      name and the glyph here still say WHICH season, so the colour is never the only signal.

      The undated block has no season and no year, so it prints its own label and no chip. A year
      whose season nobody remembers (`yearOnly`) prints "Season unknown" and no glyph, and its chip.

      HISTORY says how long ago it was, in the chip beside its year ("Year 1237 · 10 years ago"):
      `agoLabel`, set only on years from before play (timeline-view.js#agoLabel).

      WHAT THE SEASONS CHANGE RECORDED prints under the name (`seasonNotes`, timeline-view.js): the
      gains, the Surplus and any notes, IN the heading rather than as a card filed under it, which
      only repeated the season's name (user's call, 2026-10-03). Each note is still a stored row, so
      it carries the row's id and thread for the window's Edit and Remove; a host that cannot write
      (the journal page) hands `canEdit` false and gets the words alone. A host with notes wears
      `stonetop-timeline-head--notes`, which turns a pill-shaped heading into a box they fit in.

      THE NAME IS CENTRED ON ITS CAPITALS beside the glyph (user, 2026-10-04: "Summer" sat 1-1.5px
      low in its chip). The glyph is a flex item, not an inline picture lowered into the line, and
      the name's own span is trimmed to its cap band (a bare text node is an anonymous flex item,
      which takes no `text-box`).

      Context: one period view-model (timeline-view.js#periodVM). --}}
<h3 class="stonetop-timeline-period-title{{#if glyphClass}} stonetop-season-entry {{glyphClass}}{{/if}}">
	<span class="stonetop-timeline-period-name">{{#if undated}}{{label}}{{else}}{{seasonLabel}}{{/if}}</span>
</h3>
{{#unless undated}}
<span class="stonetop-year-chip">{{yearLabel}}{{#if agoLabel}} &middot; {{agoLabel}}{{/if}}</span>
{{/unless}}
{{#if seasonNotes.length}}
<div class="stonetop-timeline-season-notes">
	{{#each seasonNotes}}
	<div class="stonetop-timeline-season-note" data-entry-id="{{id}}" data-track-id="{{trackId}}">
		{{#if title}}
		<p class="stonetop-timeline-season-note-title">{{title}}</p>
		{{/if}}
		{{#if enrichedBody}}
		<div class="stonetop-timeline-season-note-body">{{{enrichedBody}}}</div>
		{{/if}}
		{{#if canEdit}}
		<div class="stonetop-timeline-card-actions stonetop-timeline-season-note-actions">
			<button type="button" class="stonetop-timeline-edit" data-entry-id="{{id}}"
			        aria-label="{{localize "stonetop.timeline.editSeasonNote"}}"
			        data-tooltip="{{localize "stonetop.timeline.editSeasonNote"}}"
			        data-tooltip-direction="UP"><i class="fas fa-pen"></i></button>
			<button type="button" class="stonetop-timeline-remove" data-entry-id="{{id}}"
			        aria-label="{{localize "stonetop.timeline.removeSeasonNote"}}"
			        data-tooltip="{{localize "stonetop.timeline.removeSeasonNote"}}"
			        data-tooltip-direction="UP"><i class="fas fa-xmark"></i></button>
		</div>
		{{/if}}
	</div>
	{{/each}}
</div>
{{/if}}
